\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Uniqueness test over 28 entities, with 95\% cluster bootstrap intervals over (entity, template) cells. Only b's gap excludes zero. Note the asymmetry in precision: the control mean rests on 162 cells and is tight, while a single entity rests on 6 and is not --- which is why the \emph  {gap} is well determined even though the per-entity intervals are wide.}}{4}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:wide}{{2}{4}{Uniqueness test over 28 entities, with 95\% cluster bootstrap intervals over (entity, template) cells. Only b's gap excludes zero. Note the asymmetry in precision: the control mean rests on 162 cells and is tight, while a single entity rests on 6 and is not --- which is why the \emph {gap} is well determined even though the per-entity intervals are wide}{table.2}{}}
